            <ArticleTitle>[Acute and recurrent night leg pain in young children: &quot;growing pains&quot;].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>363-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Acute nocturnal and recurrent pain of the limb in children or &quot;growing pains&quot; constitute a poorly known pathological entity. Growing pains occur in 20% of children aged 2 to 12. The diagnosis is made after ruling out all organic pathology: inflammatory, infectious, post-infectious, traumatic, metabolic, tumoral, vascular, hematologic, orthopaedic and benign pathology of children. The treatment requires analgesics and soft massage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
